                            <comment id="16518083" author="ivanan.fed" created="Wed, 20 Jun 2018 12:08:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ein&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ein&quot;&gt;ein&lt;/a&gt;, Hi!&lt;br/&gt;
I investigated  this issue and found that locally tests failed only when ssh disconnected per timeout. I assume that ssh timeout on TeamCity could be set incorrectly: as one of StartStopNodes tests is started, ssh could be disconnected per timeout.  &lt;br/&gt;
Change ssh timeout on server side is easy, we should add some lines in ~/.ssh/sshd_config file: &lt;br/&gt;
ClientAliveInternal n - the server send the clients &#171;null packet&#187; every n seconds to keep connection alive,&lt;br/&gt;
ClientAliveCountMax m - &#171;null packet&#187; will be send m times.&lt;br/&gt;
I suppose that it can fix flucky tests on ssh connection. What do you think?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
