                            <comment id="16527375" author="ivanan.fed" created="Fri, 29 Jun 2018 10:03:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vveider&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vveider&quot;&gt;vveider&lt;/a&gt;, as I understood process of the start node:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;We connect to remote node in java via ssh with&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/blob/master/modules/ssh/src/main/java/org/apache/ignite/internal/util/nodestart/StartNodeCallableImpl.java#L128&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;JSch&lt;/a&gt; API in Java. For this we create session with&#160;determined username, host, port and password&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;We &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/blob/master/modules/ssh/src/main/java/org/apache/ignite/internal/util/nodestart/StartNodeCallableImpl.java#L313&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;create&lt;/a&gt; shell channel on this Session object to transfer command which launches Ignite on this node via ignite.sh. After that we wait for 1000&#160;milliseconds until node launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;So we connect via ssh with Java and launch node via shell script.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
